.TH ZZ9000 7 "15 November 2026" "amix-z3660rtg" "Devices"
.SH NAME
zz9000 \- RTG framebuffer of the Z3660 and of MNT ZZ9000 cards
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /dev/zz9000
.br
.B /dev/zz9000i
.br
.B /dev/zz9001
.br
.B /dev/zz9001i
.br
.B #include \(dqzz9000.h\(dq
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B z3660rtg
module drives the RTG output of the Z3660 accelerator and of MNT ZZ9000
cards, Zorro II and Zorro III.
It is a loadable kernel module of the demand class on character major 49:
it loads at the first open of one of its nodes, after the
.BR monsw (7)
module it depends on, and finds every supported board.
.PP
Unit 0
.RI ( /dev/zz9000 ,
minor 0) is the first board, unit 1
.RI ( /dev/zz9001 ,
minor 1) the second.
The Z3660's onboard RTG is always unit 0; a ZZ9000 card beside it is unit 1.
With one board, unit 1 answers
.BR ENXIO .
.PP
The device is the board's framebuffer:
.BR read (2),
.BR write (2)
and
.BR mmap (2)
reach it from offset 0, never the board's registers.
The X server
.RB ( Xzz9000 )
maps it; the ioctls of
.I zz9000.h
set the mode and the pan, switch the output, fill and copy rectangles, and
run the framebuffer console.
The registers the display uses are reached through
.B ZZ9KIOC_GETREG
and
.B ZZ9KIOC_SETREG
only, and only those; the rest of the register page (the firmware's
ethernet, USB, SD and update registers) is refused.
The node is mode 0660, owner root, group sys.
.PP
The information node
.RI ( /dev/zz9000i ,
minor 128;
.IR /dev/zz9001i ,
minor 129) is mode 0444.
It answers
.BR ZZ9KIOC_GETINFO ,
.BR ZZ9KIOC_GETFBINFO ,
.BR ZZ9KIOC_GETMODES ,
.B ZZ9KIOC_SENSORS
and the monitor-switch Get, and nothing else.
.SS Which board
.B ZZ9KIOC_GETINFO
gives
.B zorro
and
.BR product ,
which together name the board:
.TP 12
.B "3 and 1"
the Z3660's onboard RTG
.RB ( ZZ9K_IS_Z3660 );
.TP
.B "2 and 3"
a ZZ9000 card as a Zorro II board
.RB ( ZZ9K_IS_ZZ9000_Z2 );
.TP
.B "3 and 4"
a ZZ9000 card as a Zorro III board
.RB ( ZZ9K_IS_ZZ9000_Z3 ).
.SS The monitor
A ZZ9000 passes the Amiga's own picture through its output, so one monitor on
the card shows both.
The driver switches the card to RTG when the X server asks for the RTG
display, to the Amiga picture when it gives the display back, and to the Amiga
picture at the last close of the node, so an X server that exits or is killed
leaves the Amiga picture, unless the framebuffer console is shown on that
board.
A machine whose monitor is switched by a separate line uses
.BR monsw (7)
as well; the Z3660 has no pass-through and uses only that.
.SS A board above 1 GB
A Zorro III board lies above the kernel's identity-mapped first gigabyte.
The module maps its register page and the start of its framebuffer for the
kernel (the
.B kvfb
parameter); user
.BR mmap (2)
reaches the whole framebuffer.
.BR read (2),
.BR write (2)
and the kernel's own drawing reach only the mapped part.
On the 68030 line the mapping comes from a small pool the whole kernel shares:
with the default 2 MiB a ZZ9000's framebuffer console takes 1280x720 instead
of its 1920x800 and says so;
.B kvfb=3
gives it the full mode.
On the 68040/68060 line the mapping comes from the kernel's virtual arena,
which the kernel heap shares; the default request (8 MiB) is more than the
arena has free, so it halves, and the attach line prints what was mapped
(typically 4 MiB).
The console then fits but scrolls by copying the screen instead of panning.
.SH PARAMETERS
Set in
.I /etc/conf/modreg.local.d/z3660rtg
as
.BI "param " name = value
lines (see
.BR kbootset (1M)).
.TP 10
.B blit
1 (the default): fills and copies use the card's blitter where the driver
uses it (the Z3660); 0: the CPU.
The ZZ9000's blitter is not used.
.TP
.B fixed
0 (the default): the Z3660 is found through its AutoConfig entry, as on a
real machine; 1: its fixed base at
.B 0x10000000
is also tried, which emulators without that entry need, but only when the
AutoConfig list holds the Z3660 (manufacturer 0x144B, product 1): on a machine
without one the base is not read, and the console says so.
.TP
.B kvfb
MiB of the framebuffer of a board above 1 GB mapped for the kernel, 1 to 46;
0 (the default) is the line's default, 8 on the 68040/68060 line and 2 on the
68030 line.
A request the kernel cannot meet is halved until it can, down to 1.
.TP
.B maxarea
Pixels per blitter band (0 is the default, 8192): the CPU waits in one
register write for a whole band and takes no interrupt meanwhile.
.SH FILES
.TP 20
.I /dev/zz9000
unit 0, the first board
.TP
.I /dev/zz9000i
its information node
.TP
.I /dev/zz9001
unit 1, a second board
.TP
.I /dev/zz9001i
its information node
.TP
.I /etc/conf/mod.d/z3660rtg
the module
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR monsw (7),
.BR ztop (1),
.BR kbootset (1M)
.SH NOTES
The ZZ9000 support follows the card's firmware source (ZZ9000OS 2.9.1);
older MNT firmware has not been checked.
